The `getEstimatedTickCount` function doesn't handle edge cases properly:
1. If `intervalMs` is 0 or negative (when `every` is 0 or the interval is invalid), this will return `Infinity` or a negative number
2. If `minTime > maxTime` (invalid time range), `timeDiffMs` will be negative, resulting in a negative tick count

Consider adding validation:
```javascript
function getEstimatedTickCount(minTime, maxTime, every, interval) {
  if (every <= 0 || minTime > maxTime) {
    return Infinity;
  }
  const timeDiffMs = maxTime - minTime;
  const intervalMs = dayjs.duration({ [interval ?? 'day']: every }).asMilliseconds();
  if (intervalMs <= 0) {
    return Infinity;
  }
  return Math.ceil(timeDiffMs / intervalMs);
}
```
