The `parseInt` call should validate that the result is not `NaN`. If `resultTickInterval[1]` contains non-numeric characters, `parseInt` will return `NaN`, which will then be passed to `getEstimatedTickCount` and `dayjs.duration`, potentially causing issues. Consider adding validation:
```javascript
const every = parseInt(resultTickInterval[1], 10);
if (isNaN(every) || every <= 0) {
  log.warn(`Invalid tick interval value: "${resultTickInterval[1]}". Skipping custom tick interval.`);
  // Skip applying custom ticks
} else {
